States were 1-2-3 in the second round, and were very close, to bring Canada the gold medal. France won the silver, while bronze went to West Germany, which had been fourth in round one, and fifth in round two. Great Britain dropped back to eighth when " [:a {:href "/athletes/11300"} "Marion Coakes"] " could not finish the second round, as her horse, " [:a {:href "/horses/2378"} "Stroller"] ", had a severe toothache. She was given the maximum points of 72.75 for her ride."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "Horse"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Faults"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Canada"] [:td {}] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CAN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CAN.png"}] "CAN"]] [:td {} "102.75"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/11929"} "Jim Elder"] " "] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/2455"} "The Immigrant"]]] [:td {}] [:td {} "27.25"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/11811"} "Jim Day"] " "] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/376"} "Canadian Club"]]] [:td {}] [:td {} "36.00"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/12011"} "Tom Gayford"] " "] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/271"} "Big Dee"]]] [:td {}] [:td {} "39.50"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "France"] [:td {}] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} "110.25"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/1